\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.   \cf0  One thing's needful! O Lord Jesus, keep  this one thing in my mind
\par \pard\li270\sl190\slmult0\qj All beside, tho 'first it please us, soon a grievous yoke we find.
\par Beneath it the heart is still fretting and striving,
\par No true  lasting happiness ever  deriving.
\par The gain of this one thing all loss can requite
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj And teach me in all things to find true delight.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.   Soul, wilt thou this one thing find thee?
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0 Seek not midst the earthly things
\par What is earthly, leave behind thee, over nature stretch thy wings.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par For where God and man both in one are united,
\par With God's perfect fullness the heart  is delighted.
\par There, there is the worthiest lot and the best;
\par My one and my all, Both my joy and my rest.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  Let my soul in full exemption
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj wake up in Thy likeness now.
\par Thou hast brought to me redemption, my sanctification Thou!
\par What ever I need for my journey to heaven,
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj By Thee, O my Saviour, is unto me given.
\par O let me all perishing pleasure forego,
\par Thy life, O Lord Jesus, alone let me know.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Jesus, Thou art my salvation
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj Thou my one, my all, shallt be.
\par Prove my fixed determination,
\par root out all hypocrisy!
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par \pard\li270\sl200\slmult0\qj Look well if on sin's slipp'ry paths I am hasting,
\par And lead me, O Lord, in Thy way ever lasting
\par This one thing is needful, all others are vain,
\par \pard     I count all well lost if I Christ may obtain.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

